    "question": "Which of the following statements correctly characterizes when a connected undirected graph has an Eulerian circuit?",
    "options": {
      "A": "All vertices have even degree.",
      "B": "Exactly two vertices have odd degree.",
      "C": "All vertices have odd degree.",
      "D": "The graph contains a Hamiltonian path."
    },
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "A connected undirected graph possesses an Eulerian circuit iff every vertex has even degree. Odd‑degree vertices prevent a closed trail that uses each edge exactly once.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
