    "question": "For a simple planar graph with v ≥ 3 vertices and e edges, which inequality must always hold?",
    "options": {
      "A": "e ≤ 2v − 4",
      "B": "e ≤ 3v − 6",
      "C": "e ≤ v + 5",
      "D": "e ≥ 3v − 6"
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "Euler’s formula for planar graphs gives v − e + f = 2, and each face is bounded by at least three edges, yielding 2e ≥ 3f. Substituting f = 2 − v + e leads to e ≤ 3v − 6.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
  {
    "question": "Which of the following degree sequences is NOT realizable by any simple graph?",
    "options": {
      "A": "5, 5, 4, 2, 2, 1, 1",
      "B": "4, 3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1",
      "C": "6, 5, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1",
      "D": "3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 1, 1"
    },
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "explanation": "Applying the Erdős‑Gallai theorem, the sequence 6,5,5,4,3,2,1 fails the inequality for k = 1 (6 > 6), so it cannot be a simple graph degree sequence.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the chromatic number of any bipartite graph that contains at least one edge?",
    "options": {
      "A": "1",
      "B": "2",
      "C": "3",
      "D": "Depends on the number of vertices"
    },
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "A bipartite graph can be colored with two colors by assigning one color to each partite set; the presence of an edge guarantees both colors are needed, so the chromatic number is 2.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  },
  {
    "question": "Let A be the adjacency matrix of a simple undirected graph G. Which entry of A³ gives the number of distinct walks of length 3 from vertex u to vertex v?",
    "options": {
      "A": "The entry in row u, column v of A³",
      "B": "The entry in row v, column u of A³",
      "C": "The sum of the entries in row u of A³",
      "D": "The trace of A³"
    },
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "For any adjacency matrix, the (i,j) entry of Aᵏ counts the number of walks of length k from vertex i to vertex j. Hence (A³)_{uv} gives the desired count.",
    "difficulty": "Medium"
  }
]
